    "text": "A charged particle having charge <math><mi>q</mi></math> and mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> moves rectilinearly under the action of an electric field <math><mi>E</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>–</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> where <math><mi>x</mi></math> is the distance in metre from the point where the particle was initially at rest. The distance travelled by the particle till it comes instantaneously to rest again for the first time, is"
